;;; world/regions/reedfen.map - Reedfen's rooms, laid out, with one intent
;;; each (harkfell-design section 8). Written before the rooms.
;;;
;;; A1 wrote the western block (A to F), A3 added G, and A4 grew the region
;;; east to its far end (H to Z; topics/harkfell-a4-region-maps in the
;;; notes). A - or | in the layout joins two rooms: their shared edge is
;;; open (the gates check it); no mark means a closed edge.
;;;
;;;   x8   x9   x10  x11  x12  x13  x14  x15  x16  x17
;;;   A -  B -  C -  G    H -  I -  J -  K -  X -  Y     y3  the surface
;;;   |         |         |              |    |    |
;;;   D -  E -  F -  L -  M -  N -  O -  P    Q -  Z     y4  the under-fen
;;;                            |    |
;;;                            W -  V                    y5  the drowned
;;;
;;; The surface cannot pass the Old Stone's wall (G, behind it, opens only
;;; to H2), so the way east goes under it: down C's hole to F, over F's
;;; shelf into L, and up the Root Stair (M) into the sky again at H. The far
;;; fen runs east to the Heron's Water (X), too wide to cross above; its
;;; water goes down into Q, a swim east to Z, whose roots climb to the Far
;;; Mound (Y) and H2. Under the surface a second way runs east through the
;;; roots (M to P, and up the Seep to the Cattails), with a loop down to the
;;; Drowned Bell (N, W, V, O). Home is either way back.
;;;
;;; Breaths: B, D, G, H, K, O, V (seven of twenty-two).
(map
  region: reedfen
  origin: (8 3)
  layout:
  ("A-B-C-G H-I-J-K-X-Y"
   "|   |   |     | | |"
   "D-E-F-L-M-N-O-P Q-Z"
   "          | |      "
   "          W-V      ")
  rooms:
  ((A "Fen Edge" "you step off the Hollow's rim and the land opens into reeds and sky")
   (B "Reed Bridge" "the first open water; a breath after the Hollow's climbs")
   (C "Old Stone" "a mute stone seen before it can matter, across a gap that needs a run")
   (D "Root Hollow" "a breath under the reeds: low, dark and still, found by falling")
   (E "Drowned Channel" "too wide to jump: the first swim, bank to bank")
   (F "Climb Back" "rough rock taught where a fall costs nothing, then the climb home to the stone")
   (G "Behind the Stone" "the first place a harmonic opens: a sheltered hollow where moths come to what you carry")
   (H "Stone's Shadow" "back under the sky behind the Old Stone's wall: a breath, and the fen opens east")
   (I "Frog Choir" "a round pool ringed by bellfrogs: the choir's room")
   (J "Stepping Stones" "tussocks across brackish water: short hops, and one that needs a run")
   (K "Cattails" "tall reeds gone to seed, the down drifting on the wind: a breath")
   (X "The Heron's Water" "the widest water, too wide to cross above: the way on is down through it")
   (Y "The Far Mound" "the fen's far end under the whole sky, and the note you followed, lying on the mound")
   (L "Under the Stone" "the low way east beneath the Old Stone's wall, found over the Climb Back's shelf")
   (M "Root Stair" "roots to climb from the dark back up into the sky")
   (N "Dripping Roots" "a low cave of roots under the frog pool, where its water drips through: the way down to the steps")
   (O "Root Hall" "a long low hall of roots where moths drift: a breath in the dark")
   (P "The Seep" "wet rough rock beside a falling trickle: the climb up to the cattails")
   (Q "Under the Heron's Water" "a long swim beneath the widest water to the far bank")
   (Z "The Mound's Roots" "the last climb, through roots, up to the far mound")
   (W "Drowned Steps" "old steps going down into still water: the way to the bell")
   (V "The Drowned Bell" "a bell the old people sank, hanging in deep water: swim down and listen"))
  ;; A4: the Fen Edge's west edge opens onto the Hollow's Rim (x7y3)
  borders: ((A west)))
